.TH ROOM 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
room \- Carve a room at explicit coordinates and enter it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B room
.I x y z w
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Create the room at coordinates
.IR x ,
.IR y ,
.IR z ,
.IR w ,
or find it if it already exists, and enter it. Each coordinate is a signed
number within the short range; anything else is a usage error.
.PP
Every carved room otherwise inherits its world from the room it was carved
from, so without this command no non\-zero world is reachable in play. The
explicit coordinates are the point: they name a world directly.
.PP
You must rule the region the target position falls in, or an ancestor of
it; a neighbour's ruler cannot be reached around through this command. The
command reports the room back, saying whether it was newly carved or already
there.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR planet,here,teleport (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
